diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 157309b4aa6a12da351764582fac03be445f3054..7278594ee7890eb89effc1b91a05bde866e34b8a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -10,3 +10,8 @@ Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 Discount codes: `orders.applyCode(number, code)` gives an order `SPRING10` (10 % off the items, half a cent rounds up)
 or `WELCOME5` (5.00 € off items of 30.00 € or more). An order has one code at most; a new one replaces the old. Shipping
 is never discounted, and free shipping is still decided on the items before the discount. `totals` shows `discountCents`.
+
+Monthly export: `orders.exportMonth('YYYY-MM')` gives CSV text for the accountant: a header line, then one line per
+order placed in that month, by number, with the columns `order`, `date`, `customer` (the name only: never email or phone) and `total`
+(what the customer pays after discount and shipping, in euros, such as `12.50`). Values with a comma, quote or line
+break are quoted. A month without orders gives the header alone; a month that is not `YYYY-MM` is refused.
